    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\nThe change request was to \"show money properly everywhere \u2014 a dollar sign and cents, like `$100.00`.\" As the spec itself notes, this is a UI-display-only change (amounts are still stored/audited as raw numbers, e.g. the paid-invoice audit still records `amount=100.00`), so no schema or server change was warranted.\n\nI made it additive and consistent across the app:\n\n- **New file `ui/money.ts`** \u2014 a shared `formatMoney()` primitive that renders any amount as `$100.00`, so every monetary figure formats identically without per-feature branching (CLAUDE.md's `ui/` rule).\n- **`features/invoices/InvoicesTable.tsx`** \u2014 the per-invoice `invoice-amount` and the `project-invoices-total` now go through `formatMoney`.\n- **`features/dashboard/DashboardSummary.tsx`** \u2014 the `dashboard-outstanding-total` uses it too, so money reads `$\u2026` everywhere it surfaces, not just the two testids the spec asserts.\n\nAll existing `data-testid`s are untouched, frontend typecheck passes, and `bin/e2e` reports 1 passed.",
